\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God of our fathers, known of old,
\par Lord of our far-flung battle line,
\par Beneath whose awful hand we hold
\par Dominion over palm and pine-
\par Lord God of Hosts, be with us yet,
\par Lest we forget-lest we forget!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The tumult and the shouting dies,
\par The captains and the kings depart;
\par Still stands Thine ancient sacrifice,
\par A humble and a contrite heart.
\par Lord God of Hosts, be with us yet,
\par Lest we forget-lest we forget!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Far-called, our navies melt away,
\par On due and headlines sinks the fire;
\par Lo, all our pomp of yesterday
\par Is one with Nineveh and Tyre!
\par Judge of the nations, spare us yet,
\par Lest we forget-lest we forget!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If, drunk with sight of power, we loose
\par Wild tongues that have not Thee in awe,
\par Such boasting as The Gentiles use,
\par Or lesser breeds without the law-
\par Lord God of Hosts, be with us yet
\par Lest we forget- lest we forget!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For heathen heart that puts her trust
\par In reeking tube and iron shard
\par All valiant dust that builds on dust
\par And guarding, calls not Thee to guard:
\par For frantic boast and foolish word-
\par Thy mercy on Thy people, Lord!
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

